Found by mcp-hub-binary-worker during k28. The handshake logs 'IO::Socket::SSL 2.009+ required', but agents keep getting the 503 still-fetching meaning instead of a failed upstream — against the hazard '404/401/503 carry meaning'. Happens in a minimal CPAN install and in the Docker image too: neither cpanfile nor Dockerfile carries IO::Socket::SSL. Related: the open maintainer question whether the standalone binary packs TLS (k28).

From k36 (2026-11-03): the packed binary now always carries IO::Socket::SSL 2.009+, Net::SSLeay with static OpenSSL 3.5.9 and Mozilla::CA, so k32 cannot occur there — CPAN installs still can. Binary worker recommends 'requires IO::Socket::SSL, 2.009' in the cpanfile (Mozilla::CA stays binary-only); then the Docker build stage may need libssl-dev/zlib1g-dev (the local raudssus/mcp-hub:latest already has IO::Socket::SSL 2.099, not from the cpanfile; a fresh build is unchecked). The README 'Requirements' section does not mention IO::Socket::SSL for https.

Maintainer decision 2026-11-04: IO::Socket::SSL becomes a hard requirement ('requires IO::Socket::SSL, 2.009' in the cpanfile); the Docker build stage gets whatever it needs to build Net::SSLeay (check a fresh build). k32 is still fixed so that an https upstream without TLS fails loudly with a clear reason instead of answering 503 forever.

2026-11-04 02:40 Reproduced (MOJO_NO_TLS=1, https url at a local plain TCP listener): state stopped, every tools/list 503 'not ready yet'. Cause: the warming fetch fails once, the upstream goes back to stopped, and _route_server answers 'not ready yet' while no manifest exists; nothing ever retries. Fix: Upstream::Http->new dies when the url is https and Mojo::IOLoop::TLS->can_tls is false, so _build_upstream keeps the entry as a failed placeholder whose reason names the fix (install IO::Socket::SSL 2.009+, leave MOJO_NO_TLS unset, restart). Placeholder rather than an in-object failed state: TLS is a compile-time constant of Mojo::IOLoop::TLS, so no refresh or reload can cure it, and placeholders are the hub's existing 'unbuildable entry' path. Docker: perl:5.40-slim (trixie) already ships IO::Socket::SSL 2.099, Net::SSLeay 1.96, libssl-dev and zlib1g-dev (apt-mark showmanual), as do 5.38-slim, 5.40-slim-bullseye and 5.42.3-slim-trixie, so no apt change, only a comment. Fresh --no-cache build running.

2026-11-04 02:54 Also found (for this board, not fixed): (1) any upstream whose single warming fetch fails stays 'stopped' with no error and answers 503 'not ready yet' indefinitely, because nothing retries until a refresh. Verified with a stdio {command: false} and an http url at a dead local port. k32 fixes only the TLS case, where retrying cannot help anyway. (2) A compose entry with an explicit https url builds its Docker::Http engine with url undef and sets it at start, so the build-time TLS check does not cover it; without TLS it fails at start with Mojo's 'IO::Socket::SSL 2.009+ required' through compose's own failure path. (3) The mcp-hub-runtime skill's Http section does not mention the TLS precondition, which an optional skill update could add.

